ent":"Horizontal pastel of white, grey, and grayish-blue wave-like formations with areas of the paper exposed.  In the center is a grey-blue triangular shape, and below it on the page are rippling lines of grey on white.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"(Alfred Stieglitz, New York, N.Y.) \nSherwood Anderson, New York, N.Y., by 1923 \nMr. \u0026 Mrs. Robert L. Anderson, Marion, Virginia, 1941, bequest \nRobert Lane Anderson, Marion, Virginia, 1951, bequest (Source: Lynes, 1999)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. The White Wave, 1922. Pastel on paper, 19 x 25 inches. Private Collection. © Georgia O'Keeffe Museum. [L.1998.3.1]","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"The White Wave, 1922","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Private Collection","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Pastel on paper, 19 x 25 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"19 x 25  inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Double entries Downtown Gallery Archive. Whitney Archive (American Art Research Council Questionnaires), Abiquiú Notebooks indicate, \"on back: 'The White Wave' by Georgia O'Keeffe. Pastel 1922 Exhibited 1923 Anderson Gallery. Property of Sherwood Anderson\" [not verified]. Abiquiú Notebooks indicates, \"O'Keeffe dates it to 1921. Betty Pilkington 1957.\" Abiquiú Notebooks dates 1921. Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive, date 1922. Pictured in 1923 New York (Anderson) Stieglitz installation photographs, see Appendix III, figures 12, 16. See cat. nos. 381, 382, 384–87. (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/713792/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/713792"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}